io and the red thing is... no.\n\nLet me just do get_region object at (120,70) and at (145,70) and see.\n\nHmm, get_region color mode might be better: it selects connected pixels of one palette slot. If the green blob uses bg palette 0 slot 1 ($29 lime), get_region color would select all bush-green pixels.\n\nHonestly, the cleanest: list_sprites already tells me the only sprites. There is NO Koopa on screen now. So I should move forward to where the Koopa is. The green blob is probably a bush background tile and my coordinate estimate is off; not important.\n\nBut wait: is the Koopa ahead or behind? The task says at ~1650 (page 6). We're at page 5 low 237 = 1517. Page 6 starts at 1536. So the Koopa is just ahead, about 130px. Let me step forward ~60-90 frames (100-150px) and screenshot, then pause.\n\nBut if the Koopa walks left toward Mario, it might already be near. Since we're invincible, touching it won't kill Mario. It would turn around.\n\nLet me advance carefully: play_input [{right,b} 40] → +60px → x1577. Then screenshot. Then more.\n\nHmm, but I don't want to overshoot. Let me do 30 frames (~50px) and screenshot.\n\nActually, let's reconsider: the task says \"an earlier session found it at about level x 1650 (page 6), and it appears as the camera nears it\". So the Koopa spawns when the camera nears x1650. At camera 1401 it may not have spawned yet. Advancing Mario to ~1600 (camera ~1470) might spawn it.\n\nLet me do play_input [{right,b} 45] (~70px → x1587), then screenshot + list_sprites.\n\nHmm, but each screenshot is a turn. Let me combine: play_input then in same message screenshot? Order issue. \n\nAlternative: play_input with watch on $0086/$006D and I can judge. Then screenshot.\n\nLet me run 40 frames.\n\nActually, wait — I realize the green blob might indeed be the Koopa Troopa, and list_sprites might not list it because... hmm, no.\n\nLet me test one thing quickly: read OAM at OAM index 30-40 via read_memory oam. But list_sprites is authoritative