he sprite routine reads $39 only at spawn.\n\nHmm, OR maybe because $39 needs to be set BEFORE the item rises out (and it's too late). The item rises for ~32 frames. We wrote $39=2 at 6 frames after the hit (jump 30 frames, hit ~frame 10, then 6 frames). Actually the item may have already been spawned.\n\nHmm, but the item was still inside/at the block. Changing $39 at that point should be \"before the item comes out\". Yet the sprite stayed mushroom. So the sprite uses a different byte.\n\nLet me find the sprite-selection byte. Ideas:\n- The powerup sprite tiles might be read from the object's type via a table. If $0016=0x2E for the powerup, then the sprite routine probably checks $39 to pick tiles (mushroom/star). Hmm.\n\nLet me look at the powerup object handler. Find code that reads $39: we saw $BC95 (movement) and $D80C (pickup). The sprite drawing for the powerup is elsewhere.\n\nLet me search for \"A5 39\" (LDA $39) in prgRom.\n\nLet me do search_memory hex \"A5 39\".\n\nThat gives all readers of $39. Then disassemble around them.\n\nLet me batch: search \"A5 39\" and search \"A9 2E\"."}
