{"type":"text","text":"Both metasprites are mapped and promoted (0 hypotheses skipped). The emulator is paused on the starman frame.\n\n## `koopa` — Koopa Troopa (green shell)\n\nReached by playing: from a real 1-1 start (attract demo → title → Start), I set the star timer `$079F = 200` for safety and ran right+B in a 30‑frame jump cycle. He jammed on the tall pipe at ~x 900, so I backed off 30 frames with Left and took a running jump over it; stopped at level x 1629 (page 6) with the Koopa on screen.\n\n`list_sprites` proof (OAM 18–23, origin (177,185), 16×24, sprite palette 5, no flip_v, behind_background = false):\n- `$A5` (+0,+0) flip_h · `$FC` (+8,+0) flip_h (blank filler) · `$A7` (+0,+8) flip_h · `$A6` (+8,+8) flip_h · `$A9` (+0,+16) flip_h · `$A8` (+8,+16) flip_h\n\nHit‑test `list_sprites(185,196)` → OAM 21, tile `$A6`, palette 5, opaque; `get_region` object = 213 sprite‑palette‑5 pixels, box (177,186)–(192,208), CHR `$A5`–`$A9`.\n\n## `starman` — star / invincibility power‑up\n\nThe emerging item's type is zero‑page **`$0039`**: the power‑up sprite routine at CPU `$E6E2` does `LDX $39` and picks a 4‑tile group from the PRG table at CPU `$E6BE` (X=0 mushroom `$76–$79`, X=1 flower `$D6/$D9`, **X=2 starman `$8D/$E4`**). I bumped the brick‑row mushroom ?-block at level x 336, and while the mushroom was still on it wrote `$0039 = 2` — the item redrew as the starman.\n\n`list_sprites` proof (OAM 42–45, origin (186,130), 16×16, sprite palette 7, behind_background = true, no flip_v):\n- `$8D` (+0,+0) no flip · `$8D` (+8,+0) flip_h · `$E4` (+0,+8) no flip · `$E4` (+8,+8) flip_h\n\n`get_region` object at (192,134) = 112 sprite‑palette‑7 pixels across OAM `#42–#45` (CHR `$8D`/`$E4`), box (187,130)–(200,143); `get_pixel_color(196,141)` = brown (`$17`). Note: writing `$0039 = 2` *before* the bump doesn't survive — the block‑spawn code at CPU `$BC6B–$BC79` rewrites `$0039` from `$0756`.\n\nBoth entries (with the full OAM tile/offset/flip/palette lists and reach instructions) are now in the ROM's sprite mappings."}
